<title>UK: POLYGRAM 96 NET INCOME FALLS 2.6 PCT.</title>
<headline>POLYGRAM 96 NET INCOME FALLS 2.6 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million guilders unless stated)</p>
<p>Net income pre </p>
<p>  extraordinary items     722		    vs 741</p>
<p>Net income after </p>
<p>  extraordinary items     608		    vs 741</p>
<p>Net income per share</p>
<p>  pre extraordinary items 4.01		   vs 4.12</p>
<p> Dividend (guilders)	0.95		   vs 0.95</p>
<p> Net sales		    9,488		  vs 8,798</p>
<p> Gross income		 4,571		  vs 4,256</p>
<p> Income before tax	  1,070		  vs 1,082</p>
<p>NOTE - PolyGram said in October its 1996 results would be hit</p>
<p>by a $90 million restructuring charge. Analysts had forecast net</p>
<p>income after exceptional items in a range of 585-605 million</p>
<p>guilders. Full company name is PolyGram NV. The company is 75</p>
<p>percent owned by Philips Electronics NV .</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
